  (id: "G-03", sev: "major", pri: 0, where: [GF · kitchen], req: "R-17 R-25", what: [Heavy daily cooking needs a hood of 600–900 m³/h straight outside; in a closed, positively pressurised house that flow needs make-up air, which the ERV cannot supply. The kitchen is also open to the laundry (no door), so cooking air and heat reach the maid wing.], evidence: [`east_wing.typ` fixtures: hob on the east wall, extract straight out (`DETAILS.md`); kitchen #r2(gcl("Kitchen")) m² clear, counter runs #r2(cdims(kitchen, gf-walls).at(0)) m apart; `gf-doors` kitchen ↔ laundry "open".], rule: [ASHRAE 62.2 (kitchen local exhaust 50 L/s intermittent minimum; larger hoods need make-up air, IRC M1503 above 400 cfm) · SBC 501 clause not verified; owner R-17.], fix: [A motorised make-up air damper with a filter in the kitchen's east wall interlocked with the hood; a door between the kitchen and the laundry; a grease-filtered hood 900 mm over the hob. The sink and the hob are #r2(cdims(kitchen, gf-walls).at(0) - 1.2) m apart across the room: consider the hob on the north wall or a peninsula to shorten the work triangle. Effect: the east facade (a louvre), the laundry door swing.]),
  (id: "G-04", sev: "major", pri: 7, where: [GF · maid room], req: "R-02", what: [The maid room is below the municipal minimum: #r2(gcl("Maid room")) m² clear and #r2(maid-w-north) m wide at its north end (the sloped corner), against ≥ 6.5 m² and ≥ 2.1 m. Her only way out is through the laundry and the kitchen; her window sits in the cut wall at a 1.50 m sill.], evidence: [`data/rooms_gf.csv` Maid room polygon (10.65 2.8; 11.572 2.8; 13.311 6; 13.311 6.5; 10.65 6.5): #r2(gax("Maid room")) m² on axes, #r2(gcl("Maid room")) m² clear; `PROJECT_V6.md` §4.9 ("the earlier 6.5 m² target is dropped"); window (12.17, 3.9)–(12.714, 4.9) sill +1.50 (`3d/params.yaml`).], rule: [MOMAH villa requirements 2024: driver's / maid's room ≥ 6.5 m² and ≥ 2.1 m wide (reported); emergency escape from a sleeping room: an openable window with its sill ≤ 1.12 m (IRC R310, on which SBC 1101 is based; SBC text not verified).], fix: [Redesign the maid wing: merge the maid room with the laundry's south part (the laundry is #r2(gax("Laundry")) m² on axes) and move the washer / dryer into a laundry closet in the kitchen's north end or next to the plant area on the roof; give the room a straight wall of ≥ 2.1 m and a window with a 1.1 m sill (obscured). Effect: the kitchen's north counter, the maid's route, the cut-wall structure (RC wall W4).]),
