#block(text(22pt, weight: "bold", fill: green)[Taif / Palm House · design review V6])
#text(10.5pt, fill: luma(90))[Full review of the current design (git `main`, V6.2 with the 3D character study r2 and the air study v2.1) against the owner's requirements (`docs/REQUIREMENTS.md`), Saudi regulations and practice, and global best practice · 30 October 2026]
#v(2pt)
#warnbox[*Review only.* No design file, CSV, `base.typ` or 3D file was changed. Every figure below is computed from the project files at compile time (areas and clear areas through the presentation's helpers, widths from the studies, window heights from `3d/params.yaml`). Where a code rule could not be read from the code's own text it is marked *not verified*; the review then relies on the published summaries cited in §0.3 and on international references. This is a design review, not an engineering check: nothing here was calculated for strength, airflow or acoustics.]

#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[Overall verdict]
The plan idea is strong and already better than most Saudi villa plans: a real courtyard house, guests and family separated by one two-door passage, a west service band with one shaft, a simple concrete skeleton, a majlis of #r2(gcl("Men's majlis")) m² that seats twice the weekly guests, a living + dining of #r2(living-clear) m² that matches the brief, a master suite that follows the owner's programme, and a stair that an old person can use. The character study points the house the right way.

But the house does not yet do what the owner asked for in three places, and the three are connected. *First,* the "closed, filtered, dust-free" house is not closed: on the first floor the gallery and the family living stand open to the courtyard sky behind railings, and the double-height living has nothing above its ground-floor glass, so the room where luxury matters most is open-air (Y-01). *Second,* ageing in place is "very important" but the lift is a future store, the only showers are upstairs, the first-floor corridor is #r2(gallery-clear) m clear and the bedroom doors are 0.80 m (A-01, G-07, F-01, F-02). *Third,* the outside is not designed: no parking, no garden access from the living, the family's path to the outdoor kitchen runs through the bin yard on the lane side, no tanks, no PV, no generator, no security (S-01 … S-08, E-04 … E-06). Add two regulatory risks, the #r2(env-gap) m setback margin (S-03) and the maid room below the municipal minimum (G-04), and one decision missing from the files, the solid TV wall (G-01).

The right next step is not more detail. It is one decision, the courtyard's enclosure (open well with glazed first-floor edges, or an atrium with an operable glass roof), because it settles the dust strategy, the malqaf, the light of the living, the pergola and the first-floor plan at once. With that decided, the lift, the garden door, the maid wing and the service yard are a week's work on the plan.

#ar[*الخلاصة:* فكرة البيت قوية: بيت فناء حقيقي، فصل تام بين الضيوف والعائلة بممر ذي بابين، شريط خدمات غربي واحد، هيكل خرساني بسيط، ومجلس رجال يتسع لضعف الضيوف الأسبوعيين. لكن البيت لا يحقق بعد ثلاثة مطالب مترابطة: البيت «المغلق المفلتر» ليس مغلقا (الدور الأول والصالة ذات الارتفاع المزدوج مفتوحان على سماء الفناء)، والتقدم في العمر «مهم جدا» لكن المصعد مؤجل ولا دوش في الدور الأرضي والممر العلوي ضيق، والخارج غير مصمم (لا مواقف، لا باب للحديقة، لا خزانات ولا طاقة شمسية ولا مولد ولا أمن). القرار الأول: إغلاق الفناء، إما زجاج على حواف الدور الأول أو سقف زجاجي متحرك فوق الفناء.]

