// ================= 7 · STRUCTURE =================
= Structure and buildability
The preliminary structural study (`studies/structure.typ`, `docs/STRUCTURE_STUDY.md`) proposes a concrete skeleton with block infill, 36 columns in the wall lines (`STRUCTURE_STUDY.md` §2), spans up to #r2(calc.max(..sec.spans)) m on the courtyard lines, ribbed slabs for the 4.4–4.8 m bays, a flat 0.22 roof over the void and an upturned edge beam on the two-storey colonnade. It is honest about what it is not: nothing is calculated, and fifteen items X1–X15 wait for the engineer. The review adds nothing to the engineering; it ranks the items by their effect on the plan.
- *Decide first (they change the plan):* X5 (T-01), the soil (T-03), and the consequences of Y-01 (the roof beams R1 / R2 / R11 / R4 become a skylight frame under option B).
- *Fix on the plan side now (cheap):* X3 by moving the window (T-02); the clerestory stiffeners and the glazing heads (T-05).
- *Keep:* the scheme (T-04), the colonnade to the roof, the upturned beam (its cost is the gallery width, F-01: if the gallery is widened, B3's width is part of the answer).
#ftable(by-prefix("T-"))
#ar[*الإنشاء:* هيكل بسيط قابل للتنفيذ (أعمدة في الجدران، بحور حتى #r2(calc.max(..sec.spans)) م). البند X5 (حمل جسر سقف النادي على جدارين فوق أعصاب سقف المجلس) غير متحقق ويجب حسمه أولا؛ ولا يوجد تقرير تربة (X9). تعارض النافذة والعمود X3 يُحل بتحريك النافذة 10 سم.]

// ================= 8 · SERVICES =================
= Services and environment
== The dust strategy, as the files have it
The owner's strategy is clear: a closed house, filtered fresh air by an ERV with slight positive pressure, airtight openings. The files carry it only as a statement (`AIR_SYSTEM.md` §1, items M1–M3): the ERV is not sized or placed beyond an 11.6 m² roof reservation and the west shaft; the courtyard-facing glazing is drawn as sliding doors and full-height glass with no airtightness class; the kitchen hood (G-03) and the open first-floor edges (Y-01) break the pressure regime; and the malqaf, which the whole air study is about, supplies an outdoor space (E-01). The review's advice: let the ERV be the air system, size it now with the MEP engineer (E-02), decide the courtyard's enclosure (Y-01), and give the malqaf a job that fits a closed house or let it go.
#ftable(by-prefix("E-"))
#ar[*الخدمات والبيئة:* استراتيجية الغبار (بيت مغلق، وحدة استرجاع حرارة بفلاتر عالية، ضغط موجب) مذكورة ولم تُصمم بعد؛ شفاط المطبخ الثقيل يحتاج هواء تعويض، والملقف الجاف يصب في فناء مكشوف فلا يفيد هواء البيت المغلق (E-01: إما إبقاؤه كعنصر للفناء، أو جعل البرج مدخل الهواء النقي لوحدة التهوية، أو تهوية الأتريوم به). لا خزانات ماء ولا مولد ولا طاقة شمسية ولا أمن في الملفات. السلامة من الحريق: الدرج والممر العلوي مفتوحان على الصالة المزدوجة، فيلزم كواشف دخان مترابطة ومنفس دخان أعلى الفراغ، ويُنصح برشاشات سكنية.]

// ================= 9 · LUXURY AND CHARACTER =================
= Luxury and character
The owner puts luxury first in the living room and the courtyard. Luxury in those two spaces is made of four things: light, enclosure, sound and material. The design has decided the fourth (the character study: honey stone, cream plaster, warm timber, bronze, the two-storey colonnade) and left the first three open: the light of the living comes down a #r2(sky-w) m well that never sees the winter sun (G-02, Y-05); the enclosure of the courtyard and the living's upper face is undefined (Y-01); the room's acoustics are untreated (E-07). The Taif character (stone, timber, screened openings, an inward house) is right for the brief and for the Saudi Architecture Map's Taif Highlands character; the arches the owner rejected should leave the 3D (L-02).
#ftable(by-prefix("L-"))
#ar[*الفخامة والطابع:* الفخامة في الصالة والفناء تتكون من الضوء والإغلاق والصوت والمادة؛ المادة محسومة (دراسة الطابع)، والثلاثة الأخرى مفتوحة. الطابع الطائفي (حجر، خشب، مشربيات، بيت منغلق على فنائه) مناسب.]

// ================= 10 · SCENARIOS =================
= Scenarios walk-through
#let scen(title, body) = block(above: 6pt, below: 4pt, { text(9.5pt, weight: "bold", fill: green, title); linebreak(); body })
#scen([A normal day])[The family comes in by the north door from the (undesigned) parking, through the lobby and the riwaq. Breakfast in the dining, the children to school. The wife cooks in the east kitchen; the maid works kitchen – laundry – maid room and crosses the dining and the living to reach the stairs and the bedrooms. Afternoon in the courtyard: coffee on the bench under the grille, the children in the 1.0 m strips and on the steps because the pit is the only sunken floor (Y-02, Y-03). Evening TV in the living, dinner at the table; the sound rises into the gallery and reaches the bedroom doors (E-07). Nobody goes into the garden, because no family door leads to it (S-04). The ERV runs, but the first floor and the living are open to the sky (Y-01).]
#scen([Weekly men's guests with the family at home])[Guests park on the driveway beside the family's cars (S-02) and enter the west door; the foyer shows them the majlis opening at once (G-09). Coffee and dates come from the hospitality kitchen through the two-door passage: perfect. The meal is cooked in the east kitchen and carried through the dining, the living (where the family sits) and the riwaq to the passage and round to the majlis, four doors and #r1(serve-route) m away (X-01). The family's evening in the living is interrupted every time; upstairs the gym and the office sit over the majlis (F-09). The guests' WC is one (G-06).]
#scen([Relatives visiting the family])[They come by the family door, sit in the living or the women's majlis, eat at the dining table (seats 10), use the family WC (no shower, G-07). The courtyard is the family's showpiece and works for this; the women's majlis, used daily, is its second room (G-05).]
#scen([The maid's day])[Deliveries and shopping come to the kitchen service door on the east; rubbish goes out of the same door to the bins in the #r1(strip-east(7.0)) m strip (S-05); laundry in the laundry, drying on the roof — which has no stair (F-07). She cleans the bedrooms by the family stair and passes through the dining and the living to do it (X-02). Her room is #r2(gcl("Maid room")) m² and her only exit is through the kitchen (G-04).]
#scen([A dust storm])[The malqaf's damper closes, the ERV runs on its filters, the house is shut. But the gallery, the family living and the living's double height are open to the courtyard sky (Y-01): dust settles on the first-floor floors, in the sunken seating and on the living's sofa; the cleaning takes a day. Under option B (an atrium) the storm stays outside.]
#scen([A power cut in rain])[No generator point (E-05): the pumps stop (no water pressure), the fridges warm, the ERV and the AC stop, the gates and cameras go dark; the future lift, if fitted without battery lowering, stops between floors. The courtyard pit drains by gravity (good); the overflow must be sized for the storm (Y-04). With the essentials circuit and a generator in the service yard, none of this happens.]
#scen([An elderly parent staying for a week])[No ground-floor bedroom by the owner's choice: the parent sleeps upstairs. Without the lift (A-01) that means the stair twice a day (it is a good stair, A-03); the gallery is #r2(gallery-clear) m clear (F-01), the bedroom door 0.80 m (F-02), the family bath has no turning space (F-04); the only ground-floor WC has no shower (G-07). With the lift fitted, 0.90 m doors and a shower in the family WC, the week is easy.]
#ar[*السيناريوهات:* في اليوم العادي يعمل البيت جيدا داخليا لكن لا باب للحديقة من الصالة، وصوت التلفاز يصعد إلى الممر العلوي. في ليلة ضيوف الرجال يعبر الطعام غرفة العائلة بأربعة أبواب. في عاصفة الغبار يدخل الغبار الدور الأول والصالة لأنهما مفتوحان على الفناء. في انقطاع الكهرباء تتوقف المضخات والثلاجات والكاميرات لعدم وجود نقطة مولد. الوالد المسن يصعد الدرج مرتين يوميا ما لم يُركب المصعد.]

