+ *The courtyard:* an open sky well with glazed first-floor edges, or an atrium with an operable glass roof? (Y-01, the first decision.)
+ *The lift:* fitted at construction, with a roof stop? (A-01, F-07)
+ *The malqaf:* keep as a courtyard feature with its cost, turn the tower into the ERV's clean-air intake, or ventilate an atrium with it? (E-01)
+ *The garden:* a walled family terrace on the east with a door from the dining, continuing to the outdoor kitchen? (S-04, S-05)
+ *Serving the majlis:* an external covered service path and a serving door in the majlis's south-east corner, or the inside route with the family upstairs on majlis evenings? (X-01)
+ *The maid wing:* redesign to ≥ 6.5 m² and ≥ 2.1 m (where does the laundry go)? (G-04)
+ *The gallery:* widen the projection to 1.6 m (the sky well narrows to #r2(sky-w - 0.25) m) or keep #r2(gallery-clear) m with wider doors only? (F-01)
+ *Parking and arrival:* family at the north end of the driveway, guests at the south end, a screen between? A canopy at the family door? (S-01, S-02, S-07)
+ *Water and sewage:* farm well or mains, tank sizes, septic or sewer? (S-08, E-03)
+ *The safe room:* the suite dressing? (E-06)
+ *The women's majlis:* a daily family room (keep its size) or a smaller guest room? (G-05)
+ *The clerestories:* fixed acoustic glazing, giving up the stack-ventilation idea? (F-08)
+ *Sprinklers:* yes or no, given the open stair and gallery? (E-08)
